# StudySync Vietnam — environment variables
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` (local) and set the same two variables in Vercel
# (Project → Settings → Environment Variables) for production.
#
# When BOTH are present the app talks ONLY to Supabase (no sample data).
# When either is missing the app runs in DEMO MODE using local sample data.
#
# Find these in Supabase: Dashboard → Project Settings → API
#   - Project URL                      -> VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#   - Project API keys: anon / public  -> VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
# The anon key is safe to expose in a frontend; Row Level Security protects data.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI proxy — OPTIONAL. When off, the app uses the offline rule-based "AI".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# api/ai.js calls an OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint (default
# ShopAIKey). The key is SERVER-ONLY: it lives in the Vercel function and must
# NOT have a VITE_ prefix, or it would be exposed in the browser bundle.
AI_API_KEY=
# Provider base URL (must expose /chat/completions). Default shown below.
# AI_BASE_URL=https://api.shopaikey.com/v1
# Model id served by the provider (list via GET {AI_BASE_URL}/models).
# AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Public flag (safe to expose) that turns the generative AI features ON in the
# UI and routes tool calls through the /api/ai proxy. Set to "true" only once
# AI_API_KEY is configured. Leave blank/false to stay on the manual engine.
VITE_AI_ENABLED=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Offline flashcard model — OPTIONAL. When Gemini is unavailable, flashcards
# fall back to a fine-tuned T5 model that runs in the browser (transformers.js).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# By default it loads the self-hosted copy in public/models/t5-small-qg-v1 — no
# config needed. To load from the Hugging Face Hub instead (keeps the ~80 MB
# model out of your repo/deploy), push the exported model there and set:
# VITE_QG_MODEL_ID=your-username/t5-small-qg
# VITE_QG_MODEL_REMOTE=true

# Optional: lock the AI proxy to logged-in users (protects your Gemini quota).
# If BOTH are set in the Vercel env, api/ai.js verifies the caller's Supabase
# token. Same values as above, just without the VITE_ prefix.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Local note: `vite` alone does NOT run api/ai.js. Use `vercel dev` to test the
# AI features locally; otherwise the app falls back to the manual generators.
